  "regressions": [
    "Pre-main constructor, fresh child first access and TLS destructor obtain stable errno under a thread-scoped allocator returning null; exact backend call counts are checked.",
    "malloc/calloc report ENOMEM; realloc and reallocarray preserve old bytes on backend failure; posix_memalign preserves errno and output pointer on failure.",
    "C aligned_alloc/posix_memalign/reallocarray check alignment, overflow, errno and buffer preservation on ext2 and tmpfs fixtures.",
    "Plain C constructor and main linked directly to matching CRT and static std-backed libc execute with expected exit43; no Rust executable source wrapper.",
    "Native rustc builds a std hello and two proc-macro DSOs; hello and macro consumer execute successfully.",
    "Old bin/driver DSO shadowing rebuilt lib/driver caused version exit139. All copies now match, and harness rejects conflicting runtime copies before boot.",
    "Nix shell selects unwrapped Clang for header checks, avoiding host linker flags in cross-target -fsyntax-only -Werror checks."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Not a complete libc or installed C SDK; Cargo/C dependencies and standards conformance remain outstanding.",
    "Fault injection tests a null allocation backend, not physical-memory exhaustion or signal safety.",
    "RV64 guest execution not performed for this milestone; cross-build and ELF audits only.",
    "TLS header is a coordinated runtime ABI change: loader, std, compiler DSOs and consumers must match.",
    "Fresh full runtime and probe built locally; old independent static Wild linker reused. Published bundle pin unchanged."
  ],
